{"number":2139,"title":"The `task-cadence-terms` migration record probes a path #1890 moved, so it has been inert since 2026-09-14","body":"`packs/claudinite-tasks/migrations/2026-09-05-task-cadence-terms/migration.mjs` gates itself on the member's mount understanding the cadence vocabulary, by content:

```js
const CALENDAR = 'packs/claudinite-tasks/calendar.mjs';
const twoRoot = async (read, file) => (await read(`.claudinite/shared/${file}`)) ?? (await read(file));
const mountReadsBothFields = async (read) => {
  const calendar = await twoRoot(read, CALENDAR);
  …
  return Boolean(calendar) && calendar.includes('cadenceTermFor') && …;
};
```

#1890 (`1b639e3`, 2026-09-14) moved that file to `packs/claudinite-tasks/src/contract/calendar.mjs` and left no shim at the old path, so both arms of the two-root probe miss. An unreadable mount reads as "not capable" by design, so `appliesTo` has returned false — and the record has been silently inert — every night since.

**What it costs.** The record is what folds a member's own `frequency` into `preconditions` on the nightly update. It applied for the eight nights between #1733 merging (2026-09-06) and the move; a member converging for the first time after 2026-09-14 has not had its rewrite. #1732 has now closed the contract's door, so such a member's task declaration is rejected outright rather than read — the break the record existed to prevent.

**Why it is not in #2138**, the pull request that closed the door: repointing the probe makes a codemod start writing to members' own files across the fleet, which is a delivery change with its own blast radius. #1732's automerge policy was predicted from the door-removal diff, and widening it to carry a fleet-wide write would land that write under a policy written for something else.

## The fix

Repoint `CALENDAR` at `packs/claudinite-tasks/src/contract/calendar.mjs`, confirming (rather than assuming) that `SCHEMA` — `packs/claudinite-tasks/task.schema.json` — survived the same move; it did. Re-check the record's `version: '60906.9'` gate against what has since been cut: `claudinite-tasks` is at `60918.2`, so a member last converged below `60906.9` still applies the record and one past it does not, which is the behaviour the fix needs to preserve.

Pin the probe against the real tree in the same change, so the next layout move cannot silently re-inert it — a content probe whose path matches nothing reads exactly like a capable mount that simply lacks the feature, which is why this went thirteen days unnoticed.

Then sweep the other migration records for a literal `packs/claudinite-tasks/<file>.mjs` path that #1890's `src/<role>/` move invalidated. This class of bug is silent by construction: nothing fails, nothing goes red, the record just stops applying.

